{"animath":"0.1","canvas":{"height":540,"width":960},"kind":"concept","level":"secondary","scenes":[{"caption":"Friction opposes relative motion","duration_ms":9500,"id":"s1","narration":"A 60-newton push drives this block to the right. Friction fights back with 40 newtons to the left, so the net force is 20 newtons rightwards. The key: friction always opposes the relative motion — or the tendency to slide — between the two surfaces.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"Friction fights the slide","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"floor","kind":"line","stroke":"#5d6d7e","width":5,"x1":80,"x2":880,"y1":400,"y2":400}},{"at_ms":700,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#f0c27a","h":120,"id":"block","kind":"rect","stroke":"#8e5a2b","w":140,"width":2,"x":200,"y":280}},{"at_ms":1200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"push","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#c0392b","width":6,"x1":80,"x2":180,"y1":340,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":1500,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"pushL","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"push 60 N →","x":80,"y":320}},{"at_ms":1900,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fric","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#2471a3","width":6,"x1":460,"x2":360,"y1":380,"y2":380}},{"at_ms":2200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fricL","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"← friction 40 N","x":360,"y":440}},{"at_ms":2700,"do":"move","dur_ms":1800,"target":"block","to":{"x":320,"y":280}},{"at_ms":4800,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"work","kind":"latex","size":36,"tex":"F_{\\text{net}} = 60\\ \\text{N} - 40\\ \\text{N} = 20\\ \\text{N} \\rightarrow","x":80,"y":510}},{"at_ms":6200,"do":"emphasize","target":"fric"},{"at_ms":7000,"do":"caption","text":"Friction opposes relative motion — not always the motion."}]},{"caption":"Moments: force times distance from the pivot","duration_ms":10000,"id":"s2","narration":"On this seesaw, 60 newtons pushes down half a metre left of the pivot. That is a moment of 30 newton-metres. On the right, 30 newtons sits a full metre out — also 30 newton-metres. Equal and opposite moments: the seesaw balances.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"Balancing moments","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#2471a3","id":"formula","kind":"latex","size":40,"tex":"M = F \\times d","x":80,"y":170}},{"at_ms":900,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"beam","kind":"line","stroke":"#8e5a2b","width":8,"x1":180,"x2":880,"y1":340,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":1200,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#5d6d7e","id":"pivot","kind":"polygon","points":[[480,344],[440,420],[520,420]],"stroke":"#2c3e50","width":3}},{"at_ms":1600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"f1","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#c0392b","width":6,"x1":330,"x2":330,"y1":200,"y2":330}},{"at_ms":1900,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"f1L","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"60 N","x":300,"y":190}},{"at_ms":2200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"d1","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"← 0.5 m →","x":330,"y":440}},{"at_ms":2600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"f2","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#1f7a3a","width":6,"x1":780,"x2":780,"y1":200,"y2":330}},{"at_ms":2900,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"f2L","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"30 N","x":752,"y":190}},{"at_ms":3200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"d2","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"← 1.0 m →","x":610,"y":440}},{"at_ms":3800,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"work","kind":"latex","size":34,"tex":"60 \\times 0.5 = 30\\ \\text{N·m},\\quad 30 \\times 1.0 = 30\\ \\text{N·m}","x":80,"y":510}},{"at_ms":5200,"do":"emphasize","target":"pivot"},{"at_ms":6000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"bal","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"Equal and opposite — the beam stays level.","x":80,"y":120}},{"at_ms":7400,"do":"caption","text":"Moment = force × distance. Balance needs F₁d₁ = F₂d₂."}]},{"caption":"Pressure: the same force on different areas","duration_ms":9500,"id":"s3","narration":"A 200-newton crate presses on the floor. Spread over half a square metre, the pressure is 400 pascals. Put the same crate on its narrow end — 0.05 square metres — and the pressure jumps to 4000 pascals. Same force, ten times less area, ten times the pressure.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"Pressure = force over area","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#2471a3","id":"formula","kind":"latex","size":40,"tex":"P = \\frac{F}{A}","x":80,"y":170}},{"at_ms":900,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#f0c27a","h":90,"id":"crateW","kind":"rect","stroke":"#8e5a2b","w":280,"width":2,"x":120,"y":280}},{"at_ms":1200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"a1","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#c0392b","width":6,"x1":260,"x2":260,"y1":180,"y2":270}},{"at_ms":1500,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fL","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"200 N","x":290,"y":220}},{"at_ms":1900,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"area1","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"A = 0.5 m²","x":140,"y":400}},{"at_ms":2400,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#f0c27a","h":150,"id":"crateN","kind":"rect","stroke":"#8e5a2b","w":90,"width":2,"x":600,"y":220}},{"at_ms":2700,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"a2","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#c0392b","width":6,"x1":645,"x2":645,"y1":120,"y2":210}},{"at_ms":3000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fL2","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"200 N","x":675,"y":160}},{"at_ms":3400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"area2","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"A = 0.05 m²","x":560,"y":400}},{"at_ms":3900,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"work","kind":"latex","size":34,"tex":"P_1 = \\frac{200}{0.5} = 400\\ \\text{Pa},\\quad P_2 = \\frac{200}{0.05} = 4000\\ \\text{Pa}","x":80,"y":470}},{"at_ms":5200,"do":"emphasize","target":"work"},{"at_ms":6000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"ratio","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"Area ÷10  →  pressure ×10","x":560,"y":520}},{"at_ms":7200,"do":"caption","text":"Same force, smaller area — much bigger pressure."}]},{"caption":"Check the thinking","duration_ms":8000,"id":"s4","narration":"The trap here is thinking friction always opposes motion. Watch a driving wheel: the tyre pushes backward on the road, so static friction pushes the car forward — friction is helping the motion, still opposing the relative slide between tyre and road. Every number in this lesson checks out: net 20 newtons on the block, balanced 30-newton-metre moments, and a clean factor-of-ten pressure ratio.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"Check the thinking","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"myth","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"❌ “Friction always opposes motion.”","x":80,"y":170}},{"at_ms":1200,"do":"show","shape":{"cx":300,"cy":330,"fill":"#2c3e50","id":"wheel","kind":"circle","r":55,"stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":3}},{"at_ms":1500,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"tyre","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#c0392b","width":6,"x1":300,"x2":200,"y1":410,"y2":410}},{"at_ms":1800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"tyreL","kind":"text","size":22,"text":"tyre pushes back on road","x":80,"y":450}},{"at_ms":2400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fr","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#1f7a3a","width":6,"x1":300,"x2":420,"y1":360,"y2":360}},{"at_ms":2700,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"frL","kind":"text","size":22,"text":"friction pushes car forward","x":440,"y":368}},{"at_ms":3400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fix","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"Friction opposes relative slide — not motion itself.","x":80,"y":510}},{"at_ms":4700,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#2471a3","id":"cross","kind":"latex","size":26,"tex":"20\\ \\text{N},\\quad 30 = 30\\ \\text{N·m},\\quad 400 \\to 4000\\ \\text{Pa}","x":440,"y":100}},{"at_ms":5800,"do":"caption","text":"Numbers cross-check: forces, moments and pressure all agree."}]}],"subject":"science","title":"Forces: friction, moments and pressure","topic":"phys-forces"}